      "answer": "**Policy facts:**\n\n- Employees must keep credentials private, use multifactor authentication, and never share passwords or authentication prompts. [Source 1] [Source 3]  \n- If a credential is suspected to be compromised, the employee must report the incident immediately and cooperate with required actions, including a password reset, as outlined in the Security Incident Reporting Procedure. [Source 2]  \n\n**Recommendation (not policy):**  \nTo have your company password reset, follow the standard password‑reset process (e.g., use the self‑service password reset portal or contact the IT/help‑desk). If you believe your credentials have been compromised, promptly report the issue through the Security Incident Reporting Procedure described in the Information Security policy. This ensures the reset is handled securely and that any related incident is documented and investigated.",
